@@ -273,6 +273,21 @@ claims optimality, infeasibility or unboundedness.
 Rust bindings; `highs-sys` builds HiGHS from source. Each solve builds a fresh
 native model on the calling thread and destroys it before returning.
 
+Since iteration 3, settings are applied to an empty safe-wrapper-owned handle
+before importing user data. The adapter borrows the model's cost, bound and
+coefficient arrays for a single synchronous `Highs_passLp`/`Highs_passMip` call
+in row-wise (CSR) form. HiGHS copies those arrays; no borrowed pointer is kept.
+Only checked native-width index buffers and, for MIPs, an integrality buffer
+are constructed in Rust. This avoids the previous per-column growable builder
+and its extra CSC/value copies. HiGHS still converts CSR to its internal layout.
+
+`small_matrix_value=1e-12` now takes effect **before** import. Earlier versions
+set it after loading, when HiGHS could already have dropped entries at its
+initial `1e-9` threshold. Explicit zeros may legitimately be removed; an
+unexpected change in the count of nonzero coefficients raises `BackendError`.
+The same primal/dual checks, starts, cancellation and budget rules still apply.
+There is no persistent model or basis reuse and no new public setting.
+
 | `HighsOptions` field | Default | Meaning |
 | --- | --- | --- |
 | `time_limit_seconds` | `None` | cooperative budget for the whole call after validation (conversion, run, checks); HiGHS gets the remaining time as `time_limit` and the interrupt callback polls it |
